// Two declared tvars of one lambda unify in its body check (`x + y`
// over 'a and 'b). The check's rigid gate was opened through the var
// and closed through the var; the merge re-pointed the var to the
// other cell in between, so the close missed the counted cell and the
// registration image refused it. The gate holds the cells it counted.
// Both routes of both engines produce the lambda's printed type.
{let f = 'a: Number, 'b: Number|x: 'a, y: 'b| -> ['a, 'b] x + y; f}
